[ ] Generate project/provider SSH keys inside the client home when needed:
    work ssh-keygen $client <host>

== Backup readiness ==
[ ] Decide whether config-only backup is needed.
    Private encrypted target only; never this sanitized repo.

[ ] Check backup readiness:
    WORK_BACKUP_TARGET=/path/to/private-config-backup work backup-doctor

[ ] Validate config-only backup context before writing:
    sudo ~/.local/bin/work config-backup --dry-run $client /path/to/private-config-backup '<age-recipient>'

[ ] Export config-only backup from the workstation with sudo when ready:
    sudo ~/.local/bin/work config-backup $client /path/to/private-config-backup '<age-recipient>'

[ ] Confirm the private backup manifest is current:
    WORK_BACKUP_TARGET=/path/to/private-config-backup work backup-doctor

[ ] Perform a restore drill from the encrypted config backup before relying on it.

== Final validation ==
[ ] work doctor $client
[ ] work client-profile $client
[ ] work clientrc-doctor $client
[ ] work vpn-doctor $client
[ ] work tracker-doctor $client
[ ] sudo ~/.local/bin/work compliance-doctor $client   # only if applicable
EOF
}

